course: dictionary
lesson: 12029
title: Words for people who choose
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A chooser is a person who chooses. You can see the clue in the ending: -er often means a person who does something, like a teacher or a runner. «The chooser looked at all the players and picked Priya first.» Here the chooser is the one who makes the choice.
explain: Sometimes the word is part of a saying, and then its meaning is not just the person. «When we ran out of pizza, Dad said, "Beggars can't be choosers," so I ate the plain bread.» Dad is not talking about beggars. He means that when you need help, you must accept what you are given.
explain: To check a meaning, swap it into the sentence. Try "The person who chooses picked Priya first." If it still makes sense, your meaning is right. Then read the words around the saying, and you will know when it is being used.
fact: Chooser means a person who chooses.
fact: Chooser is a noun, so you can have one chooser or several choosers.
fact: «Beggars can't be choosers» means when you need help, you must accept what you are given.
fact: In games, the chooser is the person who picks the team or the players.
fact: A good check is to swap "the person who chooses" into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The chooser picked Mia first for the team.» Who is the chooser? | The team that loses | The player who runs fastest | The ball | *The person who makes the choice
exercise: «When we ran out of pizza, Dad said, "Beggars can't be choosers," so I ate the plain bread.» What does the saying mean? | *When you need help, you must accept what you are given | Only people with money can pick their food | Always eat the food you like best | Beggars should ask for pizza
exercise: Which word means a person who chooses? | choice | *chooser | chase | chosen
test: «In the game, Sam was the chooser, so he decided who went in each team.» What is the chooser in this game? | The referee who blows the whistle | *The person who picks the players | The captain who wears the band | The player who scores the most goals
test: Grandma says, «Beggars can't be choosers, so eat your carrots.» What is she telling you? | Carrots are only for beggars | Choose only the sweet food | You can pick any food you want | *You must accept what you are given
exam: Jayden says a chooser is the same as a choice. Why is he wrong? | A chooser is a verb, and a choice is a noun, so they mean the same | *A chooser is a person who chooses, while a choice is the thing that gets picked | They mean the same, so there is no difference at all | A chooser is a shop, and a choice is a bag
